# Normalize line endings for source. Without this, a Windows checkout writes CRLF
# and a Linux container writes LF, and any test that hashes a source file diverges.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.tsx  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CRITICAL: test fixtures must be byte-exact.
#
# Expo asset hashes are SHA-256 over raw file bytes. If Git applies CRLF
# conversion to a fixture (metadata.json, a JS bundle, expoConfig.json), its
# hash changes on a Windows checkout and every manifest/signature test fails
# in a way that looks like a crypto bug but is actually line endings.
# `-text` disables all conversion; `-diff` keeps binaries out of diffs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/fixtures/**   -text -diff
**/tests/fixtures/** -text -diff
*.zip  binary
*.hbc  binary
*.pem  -text -diff
